{
  "experiment": "ADR-0007 experiment 2 — runtime hydration of the Plan B candidate-COLD set",
  "measuredApps": 16,
  "rosterApps": 19,
  "failures": [
    {
      "app": "bulletproof-nodejs",
      "reason": "Two independent blockers, both materialization/upstream defects. (1) argon2's native binding is absent (MATERIALIZATION.md records this clone was installed with --ignore-scripts) and is on the startup require path; `npm rebuild argon2 --build-from-source` fails because argon2@0.27 pins node-pre-gyp v0.15.0, which does not work on Node 24, and no darwin-arm64 prebuild exists upstream. (2) Separately, tsc leaves the app's `@/…` tsconfig-path imports unrewritten and the repo ships no module-alias, so its own Procfile command cannot resolve them; that half was worked around with NODE_PATH and did resolve. The app reaches build/services/auth.js and then dies on argon2, so no startup trace is obtainable."
    },
    {
      "app": "nestjs-realworld",
      "reason": "Frozen materialization defect, not an experiment limitation: 47 top-level directories in this clone's node_modules are EMPTY (no package.json, no files) — the recorded npm \"Exit handler never called\" failure in MATERIALIZATION.md. `require(\"@nestjs/core\")` fails at the first import of the pinned entry with Cannot find module 'event-emitter', so no startup trace is obtainable. Repairing it needs a re-install, which would rewrite files INSIDE the frozen production universe and invalidate the preserved placement, so the app is reported as not-measured instead. Fixing it requires an explicit corpus revision."
    },
    {
      "app": "ghost",
      "reason": "Frozen materialization gap, surfaced by this experiment: corpus.json declares build:null for ghost, but Ghost's monorepo ships its workspace packages as TypeScript SOURCE ONLY (packages/adapters/storage-base has `main: build/index.js` and no build/), and ghost/core's own core/shared/config is index.ts. The pinned entry therefore cannot boot: first MODULE_NOT_FOUND on './shared/config', and after running the repo's own `build:tsc`, MODULE_NOT_FOUND on ghost-storage-base (an unbuilt workspace package). Making it run needs a full `pnpm nx run-many -t build` of the Ghost monorepo, which would produce a materially different tree from the one the preserved placement was computed against. The tsc output was reverted and the clone left byte-identical. NOTE: the same gap means the preserved Plan A/B numbers for ghost describe a tree that cannot execute, which is a finding about the corpus, not about virtualization."
    }
  ],
